+3. **A card check before every build.** An prior classifier breaker spends at most 15 minutes, with no heavy runs. For each observer setting the card names, it asks: does the fix change this setting's output by design, or must it hold? A mis-specified card stops here. Theorists run the same questions (`workshop/card-check.md`) over their own card before returning it, because both theorist cards failed their first check on October 15. Checks converge slowly, since each round finds finer defects. After two failed checks, or after one whose defects are all in the verdict machinery (scripts, parsers, validators) rather than in the hypotheses, variants or predictions, I may send the card to build with the check's fixes as binding notes, applied, tested and committed before any variant runs.
